  <running_head>PHYSICARUM LIB. VI.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>§.</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">maxime prævalere : quod etiam inde</l>
    <l n="2">fuadetur, quod actiones omnes in ju-</l>
    <l n="3">vene sint perfectiores, &amp; caloris sensus</l>
    <l n="4">&amp; effecta manifestiora. Has ob diffi-</l>
    <l n="5">cultates Gal. l. c. mediam sententiam</l>
    <l n="6">eligit, nempe calorem secundum gra-</l>
    <l n="7">dum in utraque ætate esse parem : at-</l>
    <l n="8">tamen secundum acrimoniam in juve-</l>
    <l n="9">ne magis notabilem, quia humido non</l>
    <l n="10">ita opprimitur. Ego tamen absolute</l>
    <l n="11">mavelim juventuti maximum calorem</l>
    <l n="12">asscribere, cujus rationes supra de cali-</l>
    <l n="13">do innato agentes expofuimus.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">§. 2. Quæstio 2. est : <i>An recte ficci-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>tatem senibus attribuerimus?</i> Ratio du-</l>
    <l n="16">bitandi est, quia Senes plurimum fri-</l>
    <l n="17">gidis humidisque humoribus scatent.</l>
    <l n="18">Cæterum contraria ratio est : quod senes</l>
    <l n="19">actione caloris paulatim siccliores</l>
    <l n="20">evadant. Atque hæc etiam vera senten-</l>
    <l n="21">tia est. Ad rationem autem oppositam</l>
    <l n="22">dicimus, quod senes illa frigida excre-</l>
    <l n="23">menta cumulent, quia ob debilitatem</l>
    <l n="24">caloris non debite alimenta conco-</l>
    <l n="25">quunt : ideoque non secundum partes,</l>
    <l n="26">quæ exsiccatæ sunt, verum tantum se-</l>
    <l n="27">cundum excrementa humidi sint.</l>
    <l n="28" type="heading" level="2" para="true">V. <i>Præternaturalis mutatio in mor-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="29" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>bis fit, atque id omnino multis modis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="30" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>speciatim vero vel congrue ad ætates, vel</i>
    </l>
    <l n="31" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>contrarie contra eosdem.</i> §.</l>
